msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:100
msgid "The town gave its chapel bell, which rang the hours for every soul in Aldwater. It still counts, under the water."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:101
msgid "It counts for you: as a chest comes to the counter, it tolls once for each thing inside, false bottom and all."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:102
msgid "The Bottled Star"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:102
msgid "twinkle"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:102
msgid "the archmages of the Keyhold"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:103
msgid "They gave a star they caught as students and kept in a bottle all their lives. Things from the Locking gather round it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:104
msgid "Starlight: enchanted things glow whenever they sound, witchlight or not, and turn up far more often."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:105
msgid "The Imp's Ember"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:105
msgid "crackle"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:105
msgid "Pib, an imp who loved a miller's daughter"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:106
msgid "He gave his own heart, a coal that never goes out, so the Maw could never have her."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:107
msgid "Tempers all it warms: glass never breaks, nothing comes out worse than promised, and fakes you open burn true."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Heartsongs.cs:115
msgid "A lock of gold could never hold the demon of greed. So at the Locking the archmages asked the peoples of Aldmark for things they loved more than gold, and sang the Locking into nine of them: the Heartsongs. Then they hid each in an ordinary chest, among millions. Only a Keywright hears one sing. To anyone else it's worth nothing, and the Guild won't touch one: greed can't put a price on it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:11
msgid "Uncle Bram"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:16
msgid "Morning! Here's the trick of it: a chest opens for you once you've paid for it, and nobody can see inside, so everyone shakes it and guesses. Pip never even shook his. Drag the chest slowly from side to side: that's a gentle shake."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:19
msgid "Your back won't take a hard shake or a drop, Hesk, but your scale doesn't lie. Weigh what you heard against what's on the scale: whatever's left over is something you couldn't hear, or something under a false bottom."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:21
msgid "Everybody haggles with you, Rosa, though they open a bit higher, knowing you. Make your offer with the slider. Too low and they'll let you try again, but walk one out of the door and they won't be back this week."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:23
#, csharp-format
msgid "Your shelf's up from the first day, Isolde. Keep what you love: visitors pay at the door every night, {0}g for every {1} points of exhibition. Just remember the Guild won't take your collection in pawn on a short night."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:25
msgid "Hear that jingle? Coin. Light things rattle at the gentlest shake. Tick Coin on your slip, there on the right."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:26
msgid "Your slip adds up what you've ticked, valued as good as the chest's colour promises. The bar underneath is your odds that it's worth more than the price: the greener, the safer."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:28
msgid "Ada only shook it gently. Nothing heavy or soft stirs for a gentle shake, so she's priced only what she heard. Try every strength yourself: gentle, firm and hard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:30
msgid "That flump is a cloak. Soft things only make a sound when you shake hard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:31
msgid "Garrick shook it hard, and when something clanks, it drowns out anything delicate. Shake it yourself, at every strength."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:32
msgid "Clank: a weapon, an axe or a blade. It only moves when you shake firmly, and while it's clanking you can't hear anything delicate. Shake gently to hear past it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:34
msgid "Bettany counts the rattles at a firm shake and charges the same for each. If you can't hear anything she didn't, pass: a seller always asks a bit more than what they've heard is worth."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:36
msgid "When you pass, they take it home unopened, and you'll never know for sure. But your gut usually has an opinion."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:37
msgid "Your mark went cold: that chest isn't theirs to sell, and it won't open for whoever buys it. Pass on it, or send for the Wardens: they pay a finder's share."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:39
msgid "Not everyone comes to sell. People have their own troubles, and what you say to them comes back: who comes, what they bring, and who's on your side. The notebook's Town page keeps track."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:41
msgid "The best tools aren't sold in shops: the people who make them bring them to the counter. Say no, and they'll ask again in a few days."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:43
msgid "A tick is a good read. A cross is something to listen for next time."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:44
#, csharp-format
msgid "That's a day's trading. Every coin goes toward the stall: once it's earned {0}g, all told, we'll talk about Thornwick."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:47
msgid "Look at the chest's colour: plain wood, green, blue, purple. The Wardens painted them by what went in, so the colour tells you how good the things inside tend to be. Only tend to: you'll get surprises both ways."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:49
msgid "See? Not everything matches its chest. Mostly it does; sometimes it's a little worse; now and then it's much better."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:50
msgid "This one names a price. Take it or leave it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:51
msgid "This one haggles, so they'll start high. Use the slider to make one offer: they'll take it, name a final price, or storm off if you insult them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:53
msgid "This one wants you to name a price. Offer what it's worth to you, less a little. You get two tries."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:54
msgid "Too low. One more try, then they'll go."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:55
msgid "Everyone you've traded with has a page in your notebook: how they judge a chest, how they trade, what they're like. Click whoever's at the counter to read theirs."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:57
msgid "Listen to where they say it came from. A barrow holds grave goods, a goblin warren mostly coin, a dwarf-hold weapons and gems."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:59
msgid "Something grand? You can keep it for display instead of selling it. A good exhibition brings more customers, and better ones. Enchanted things count double."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:61
msgid "On display. You'll see it on the shelf behind the counter."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:62
msgid "Your exhibition. Click anything in it to sell it, if you need the money."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:65
#, csharp-format
msgid "{0}g earned: the stall pays its way! Thornwick Market has more customers, richer chests and room for a shelf. But Thornwick chests cost more, so keep enough for tomorrow's. A price in red means it would leave you short: better to wait a day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:66
msgid "Nearly broke? I keep a little put by for days like this. Don't tell the Guild. It won't last forever: the day card says how much is left."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:68
msgid "A shelf behind the counter, with room for one thing! Keep something grand on display instead of selling it: an exhibition draws more customers, and better chests. Each cabinet you buy makes room for one more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:70
#, csharp-format
msgid "Crownhold folk know a shop by what it collects. Your notebook has tallied everything you've acquired: {0} of a kind earns a synergy. Open Synergies, bottom right, to put one to work or see how close you are."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:71
msgid "Another synergy slot: open Synergies and put one more to work."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:72
msgid "The Royal Emporium, in the palace's shadow. The Gate's just down the street: you can feel it hum. There are bigger things to grow into now: a night market, a patrons' book, a velvet case for curios. Keep enough back for Vane."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:74
msgid "Forgotten a sound, or someone's habits? Press N for your notebook: the sounds, the regulars you've met, and a calendar of what's coming."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:76
msgid "That's the Guild's next due, up top. Click it any time for the whole debt in your notebook: what's paid, what's left, and what each week will want."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:78
msgid "The ward's let go: the chest is yours. Now for the old lock underneath. The pick sweeps round: press {act}, or click, while it's in the green to set a pin. Set every pin cleanly and nothing inside gets scratched."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:82
msgid "Paid. Next week the Guild wants more, and more again the week after. Whatever you spend on the shop has to earn its keep before Vane comes back."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:84
msgid "Nim comes every night after closing with curios: oddments from the Locking, each bending one rule of the trade. One a night at first; his lantern brings more. Pick ones that work together: Nim notices what you buy and brings more like it. Don't ask what Nim is."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:87
msgid "The regulars want things now: see the board on the left. When something they want comes out of a chest, hand it over instead of selling it. A commission always pays more than a sale, and a lot pays piece by piece."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:89
msgid "Someone wants this! Deliver it: a commission always pays more than selling it would."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:90
msgid "Something's happening in town today: two days every week are different. It's up in the top bar (click it to read it again), and your notebook's calendar shows what's coming this week and next."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:92
msgid "The Stranger. That chest's wrapped in iron chains: nothing inside can move, so there's nothing to hear. Drop it to feel how heavy it is. Heavy ones hold more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:94
msgid "A royal seal! That's one of King Aldric's own chests, gilded. The seller thinks the gold is paint, and priced it as the colour underneath."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:96
msgid "Look at that purse: enough to pay off the whole back-tithe, every week of it, right now! Do it, and the stall is ours early. Or keep trading first: the Guild only ever asks for this week's."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:98
msgid "Short? Pawn what's on display, or your curios, at the Guild's price. If even that isn't enough, the Guild seals the shop."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:99
msgid "Short, and folk owe you a favour? Call on them first: each brings an eighth of the due, once a season. That's what friends are for."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:100
msgid "Gold! A legend, that. They're made, not mended: no restorer or lucky charm will ever turn a thing gold. It went into that chest gold."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:101
msgid "The Hooded Woman pays in shards of the Aldric Key. If you can't find what she wants this week, she'll ask again next week."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:104
msgid "Thornwick folk bring two new sounds. Potions slosh at a gentle shake, like coin. Spells (scrolls and spellbooks) rustle only at a hard shake, like cloaks. And some chests are locked, or have a false bottom. It'll be a quiet first day, while word gets round."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:107
msgid "Locked. Buy it and you'll pick the lock before you open it. A crowbar's quicker, but it breaks glass."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:108
msgid "Dropped! A solid thud means a plain chest. A hollow boom means a false bottom: something hidden that nobody's priced."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:109
msgid "Hear that boom? A false bottom. Tick it on your slip: whatever's down there, nobody's priced it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:110
msgid "Glass breaks when you drop it. If you heard a slosh, think twice before dropping."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:111
msgid "That slosh is a potion. It's delicate, like coin: a clank drowns it out."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:112
msgid "A rustle: a spell, a scroll or a spellbook. Soft, like a cloak: it only sounds at a hard shake."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:113
msgid "Crownhold brings gems, which tinkle at a gentle shake; archmages, whose things are often enchanted (a witchlight would show it); and lots with two or three of a kind. Count the rattles: click a row again for each one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:115
msgid "A tinkle: a gem. Delicate, and worth the most."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:116
msgid "The witchlight's lit, and it stays lit: anything enchanted glows when it makes a sound. Click the star on a row to mark one enchanted."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:118
msgid "Two of a kind: each one adds its value. Sellers who don't count only price one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:119
msgid "It glowed! That one's enchanted, and worth twice as much. Click the star on its row to mark it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:120
msgid "The Royal Emporium. Court folk, the Maw's creatures up through the cracks in the Gate, and Gilt, who sells demon gold: gilded iron that jingles just like the real thing. A lodestone would catch it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:122
msgid "The lodestone's on, so iron can't move. Weapons go quiet, and nothing drowns out the delicate things. Demon gold, which is iron under the gilt, goes quiet too."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:124
msgid "That's all the shaking this one will stand: it's coming apart. Go by what you heard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:127
msgid "That sound... I've heard it once in forty years. A Heartsong! Only a Keywright hears one sing, so the seller has no idea it's there. It's worth nothing in gold and everything to the shop: buy that chest. And if you can't afford it, pass: a Heartsong won't leave with them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:130
msgid "A Heartsong. Nobody would pay a penny for one, but each does something for the shop that no gold can, for as long as it sings here. Keep it or let it go: every one you keep makes the next harder to find."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:132
msgid "Hear that? The whole stall's different with it singing. It'll sing as long as it's ours."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:136
msgid "Ada only shakes gently, so heavy things and soft things make no sound for her."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:137
msgid "Tobin's Barrow chests are rotten: about two seconds of shaking, all told. One strength, then: pick it well."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:138
msgid "Nettle puts her price up a tenth for every strength you try after the first. Pick two: gentle and hard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:139
msgid "Mother Sorrel always dreams true, in signs. If you can't hear what she dreamt of, it's warded: name it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:140
msgid "A Thornwick dowry always holds coin, a cloak and a potion. Whichever of the three you can't hear is warded."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:141
msgid "Ilse's tag lists every kind of thing packed. A kind on the tag that never makes a sound is warded: name it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:142
msgid "Quire's ward-roll names the warded thing, faded. Make out the name, and tick its kind."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:143
msgid "Madame Zell's cards: a suit drawn twice is what the ward holds. Three different suits, and nothing's warded."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:144
msgid "A warded thing makes no sound and weighs nothing. Name it on your slip, and nothing that isn't there, and the ward will give it up."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:146
msgid "You could pay off the Guild now. Or buy its Bookkeeping Engine for the same sum: it reads every chest for you, to finish the run quickly."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:148
msgid "Rook's scale says what her chest weighs. Take away the weight of what you heard: what's left never stirred (a cloak is 3 lb, a spell 1)."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:150
msgid "Brass's ticket counts every article, false bottom and all. Count what you hear: one short means one under the floor."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:151
msgid "Flick's chests are mostly stolen. Lay a hand on each one: if your mark goes cold, send for the Wardens, or pass."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:153
msgid "The Guild's bailiff, selling what it took for tithe to its friends: cheap, by the colour alone. But a lot of what the Guild takes was never the Guild's to sell. Lay a hand on every one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:155
msgid "The Wardens' quartermaster sells what nobody claimed, by the pound. A heavy chest comes dear and a light one cheap: take the weight of what you hear from his scale's."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:157
msgid "Brother Cadoc won't have his chests shaken hard: half again if you do. Crypt chests are full of holy cloaks."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:158
msgid "Corvin packs his chests in straw: everything needs a strength harder to stir, and cloaks and spells won't stir at all. Shake firmly, then hard, then drop it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:160
msgid "Orme likes a wager: read her chest exactly, every kind and every count, and she gives back a third of the price."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:161
msgid "Solve grandmother's riddle. If you can't hear what it's about, it's warded: name it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:162
msgid "Sir Rowan takes the best weapon in his chest, for the fee he names. Value what's left."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:163
msgid "Tick gives you twelve seconds. Gently, then hard, and decide."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:164
msgid "Sallow is cheap, but the dearest thing inside is his. A chest of many middling things suits his bargain."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:165
msgid "Skrae's echoes come back off everything, warded or not. An echo with nothing to hear is warded."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:166
msgid "Countess Vey prices only her gems; the rest comes free. Some are paste, and she won't have a lodestone near them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:167
msgid "Old Aldo's price is your slip. Get it exactly right and he takes a quarter off; get it wrong and you pay what it holds, and a quarter more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Hints.cs:169
msgid "The Maw sells for one coin, but everyone who comes after him today asks twice as much. Count who's still waiting."
msgstr ""

