#: scripts/Core/Kin.cs:155
#, csharp-format
msgid "Rotten: it stands {0} seconds of shaking, all told."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Kin.cs:156
msgid "Packed in straw: everything needs a strength harder to stir."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Kin.cs:157
msgid "On a skittish mare: no hard shake."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Kin.cs:158
msgid "A day of mourning: no hard shake."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Kin.cs:159
#, csharp-format
msgid "Each strength you try after the first puts the price up {0}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Kin.cs:160
msgid "Read it exactly right and she gives back a third of the price."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Kin.cs:161
#, csharp-format
msgid "A contest: read it exactly right, and you win {0}g."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Kin.cs:162
#, csharp-format
msgid "The best {0} inside goes back to him, for {1}g."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Kin.cs:163
msgid "The dearest thing inside is his."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Kin.cs:164
msgid "His price is your slip: exactly right, a quarter off; wrong, what it holds and a quarter more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Kin.cs:165
#, csharp-format
msgid "Buy, and everyone after him today asks {0}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Kin.cs:165
msgid "twice as much"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Kin.cs:167
msgid "a hard shake"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Kin.cs:168
msgid "a drop"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Kin.cs:169
msgid "the lodestone"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Kin.cs:170
#, csharp-format
msgid "Minds {0}: half again if you do."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:72
msgid "Pip never shakes anything and has no idea what it's worth: he'll ask you to name a price. First, shake it at every strength."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:74
msgid "Tick what you heard. Then set the slider to a few coins and make your offer: he'll take almost anything. You get two tries."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:90
msgid "Garrick shakes hard, so a clank drowns out anything delicate for him. He haggles: he always asks about double. Shake it yourself, gently too."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:92
msgid "Tick what you heard. Then use the slider to offer him about half his price. You get one offer: much lower and he storms off."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:101
msgid "A tinker paid his tab with it. One rattle, like a fish in a crate. A rattle's a rattle: {price}, love."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:104
msgid "Bettany counts the rattles and charges the same for each, whatever's rattling: a purse of coin costs what a goblin's cleaver does. Shake it: what's rattling?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:106
msgid "A jingle: coin, worth more than any cleaver. At cleaver prices, that's a bargain."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:116
msgid "The Barrow: Tobin always says where a chest came from, and the place tells you what it tends to hold. Barrow chests hold grave goods: coin, weapons, a shroud."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:118
msgid "His chests are rotten through: about two seconds of shaking and no more. One strength, then. Hard stirs everything, but a clank would drown the coin. Shake it hard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:131
msgid "A goblin burrow: shinies her clan dug up, mostly coin. Nettle shook it gently. Do the same: the first strength is free."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:133
msgid "Every strength after that puts her price up a tenth. A gentle shake can't stir anything heavy, so pay once more for a hard one. Gentle and hard between them hear everything firm would."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:145
msgid "Rook weighs every chest on her game scale and prices by the pound. Her mare spooks at a hard shake, so nothing gets shaken hard. Shake it gently, then firmly."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:147
msgid "A slosh: a potion, 3 lb. Her scale says 6 lb, so 3 lb never sounded. A cloak weighs 3, a spell 1, and wolf dens are full of cloaks. Tick a potion and a cloak."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:163
msgid "Everyone you've traded with has a page in your notebook: how they judge a chest, and what they're like. Click Mother Sorrel to read hers."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:165
msgid "Mother Sorrel's price is a dream, but she always dreams true: of what the Wood warded in the chest, or else the dearest thing in it, as a sign. A river is a potion. Shake it at every strength."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:167
msgid "A flump and a rustle, and no slosh. The potion is warded: sealed in the ward itself, silent and weightless. Name it: tick Potions."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:169
msgid "A ward gives up only to the truth. Name what's there and nothing that isn't, and the warded thing comes out when you open the chest. Nobody priced it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:180
msgid "Brother Cadoc shook it firmly, and won't have it shaken hard: the saints are resting. Half again if you do. Shake it gently, then firmly."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:182
msgid "Crypt chests are full of holy cloaks, and cloth only sounds at a hard shake, so he never prices it. Tick Cloaks on faith, or shake it hard and pay for certainty."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:194
msgid "Corvin packs his chests in straw, so nothing clinked at the Wardens' toll. Straw muffles a strength: a gentle shake stirs nothing at all. Shake it firmly."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:196
msgid "A jingle: what a gentle shake would stir, a firm one stirs through straw. That's all he heard. Now hard: weapons stir through straw only then, and cloaks and spells never."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:198
msgid "A clank he never heard. Smugglers love a false bottom, too: lift the chest high and let go."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:199
msgid "A hollow BOOM. Tick a weapon and False bottom: he priced neither. Then haggle."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:211
msgid "Hesper sells dowries from weddings that never were. A Thornwick dowry always holds coin for luck, a cloak for warmth and a potion for health. Shake it at every strength."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:213
msgid "A jingle and a flump: luck and warmth. No slosh: the bride warded her potion, silent and weightless. Name it: tick Potions."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:223 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1006
msgid "a weaver in Thornwick"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:228
msgid "Flick runs chests for the Magpie: cheap, and in a hurry. Lay a hand on it: shake it, any strength."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:230
msgid "Your mark went cold: it isn't Flick's to sell, and if you buy it, it won't open. Send for the Wardens: Flick runs, the chest goes home, and they pay you a finder's share. Or just pass."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:244
msgid "Ilse reads the Arcanum's packing tag: it lists each kind of thing packed, and the archmages warded the most dangerous. Shake it at every strength."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:246
msgid "A flump and a rustle: the cloak and the spell. The gem on the tag never tinkled: it's warded. Name it: tick Gems."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:257
msgid "Archmage Orme wagers on your craft: read her chest exactly (every kind, every count) and she gives back a third of the price when it's open. Shake it at every strength."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:259
msgid "Tick exactly what you heard, no more and no less. A careful read takes a third off her price."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:269
msgid "Durgan's a dwarf: he knows weapons, prices the rest at half, and takes every tinkle for a diamond. Shake it gently yourself."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:271
msgid "A tinkle: a gem, and he's priced it like the crown jewels. Offer what it's really worth, or let him keep it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:281
msgid "Grandmother Vell left a riddle on each lid about one thing inside, and if she warded something, it's about that. Read it, then shake it at every strength."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:283
msgid "A hilt and an edge, or forged and sheathed: a weapon. And nothing clanked: grandmother warded it. Name it: tick Weapons."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:297
msgid "Brass sells pawn by the lot, two or three of a kind, and prices one of each kind he hears. Shake it at every strength and count: each thing sounds from its own spot."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:299
msgid "Two jingles and a rustle: three things, and he priced one purse. But the ticket counts every article pledged, and it says four. He won't have pledges dropped: the fourth is under a false bottom. Tick two Coins and False bottom."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:311
msgid "Quire sells the Archive's vault chests with their ward-rolls, faded by three hundred years. The roll names what was warded: 'B_o_d R_b_'."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:313
msgid "The Blood Ruby: a gem. Name it, and the ward gives it up when you open the chest: tick Gems."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:324
msgid "Tilly shakes hard and prices every rustle as a drowned wizard's spellbook. Shake it gently."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:325
msgid "A rustle at a gentle shake? Parchment only rustles when it's shaken hard: that's river sand pouring, worth nothing. Tick only the slosh: Potions."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:336
msgid "Sir Rowan wants his grandfather's sword. If there are weapons inside, the best of them goes back to him, for the fee he named. Shake it: is there a clank?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:338
msgid "A clank: that blade is his. Count it at his fee, not its worth, and see whether the rest pays for the chest."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:350
msgid "An imp, with an hourglass: twelve seconds, from when you close this. Things from the Maw's hoard often beat their colour. Shake it gently, then hard. Quick!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:352
msgid "Gently, then hard!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:364
msgid "A devil's bargain: Sallow's price is low, but the dearest thing inside is his. Shake it at every strength: what's in there?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:366
msgid "Four things: he takes the best, you keep three. With many middling things his bargain is a good one; with one grand thing and little else, it's his."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:377
msgid "Skrae clicks like a bat and listens to the echoes: round is coin, long a weapon, soft a cloak, hollow a potion, flat a spell, tiny a gem. Echoes come back off warded things too. Shake it at every strength."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:380
msgid "A jingle and a clank: the round one and the long one. Nothing sloshed, so the hollow one is warded: tick Potions."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:391
msgid "Countess Vey prices only her gems, at what she paid for them. Whatever else the maid packed comes free. Shake it at every strength."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:393
msgid "Tick everything you heard: the rest is a gift. Some of her gems are paste, though, and she won't have a lodestone near them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:404
msgid "Madame Zell draws three cards from the Locking's own deck: a suit drawn twice is what the ward holds; three different, nothing. Coins came up twice."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:406
msgid "So there's warded coin. Name it: tick Coin."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:416
msgid "Gilt sells demon gold: gilded iron, and it jingles just like the real thing. Turn the lodestone on and shake it gently."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:418
msgid "The jingle went quiet: iron, gilded, worth nothing. The tinkle's real: tick Gems, and leave Coin unticked."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:420
msgid "Gilt sells demon gold, gilded iron, as gold and gems, and it sounds just like the real thing. Only a lodestone can tell. Too cheap to be true, usually."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:431
msgid "Old Aldo plays a game: his price is whatever your slip says. Read it exactly and he takes a quarter off; read it wrong and you pay what it truly holds, and a quarter more. Shake it at every strength."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:434
msgid "Tick exactly what you heard, then buy. Funny: that ring of his has the royal seal on it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Lessons.cs:444
msgid "That's no merchant, Kit. That's the Maw, in a borrowed body. One coin for the chest; but buy it, and everyone after him today asks twice as much. Count who's still waiting before you say yes."
msgstr ""

