#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:357
msgid "It was stuck in the mill wheel. Mum does the mill's washing, and it came up in a sheet! How much will you give me?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:358
msgid "It was under Gran's bed. She says I can sell it if it buys Mum's soap. What's it worth?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:359
msgid "Found it in the hayloft, behind the cat. The cat didn't want it. How much?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:360
msgid "A washerwoman's boy of nine who fishes chests out of the millpond and never shakes them: he has no idea what's in one, and asks you to name a price. A few coins will do, but a millpond chest is sometimes empty."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:362
msgid "Yes! Mum can have new soap!"
