msgid "My Rafe's soldiering chest. Only a gentle shake: I couldn't bear to hear his things rattle. {price}, for Jory's debt?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:377
msgid "Rafe carried this through two wars. A gentle shake was all I could bear. {price} would help my Jory."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:378
msgid "From the attic, dear. Just a gentle shake: my wrists aren't what they were. {price}? Every coin's for Jory."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:379
msgid "A soldier's widow selling her husband's things to free her son from the Guild's debt-house. She only ever shakes a chest gently, so what's heavy (a weapon) or soft (a cloak) never makes a sound for her, and she doesn't price it. A soldier's kitbag usually holds both."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:382
msgid "Thank you, dear. That's a week off Jory's debt."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:382
msgid "Bless you. Rafe would have liked you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:383
