msgid "A young delver who goes down the Barrow to pay what the Guild says his father owed. Prices a chest by its colour and never shakes it: Barrow chests are so rotten they stand about two seconds of shaking before they start to come apart. Grave goods: coin, weapons, gems."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:431
msgid "That's another week the Guild leaves me be."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:431
msgid "Right. Back to the Barrow."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:432
msgid "Sorry, I've a barrow to get back to."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:433
msgid "Fair enough. Someone at the Crossed Keys will want it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:433
msgid "Oh well. More where that came from."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:434
msgid "Careful, it's rotten!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:434
msgid "Whoa! It'll fall apart!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:435
msgid "It's held together with damp and hope! You'll pay more for that."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:441 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:441
msgid "Nettle"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:443
msgid "Her clan cleared of every theft in Thornwick, and a burrow with a door: a goblin's worth is the chests she keeps."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:444
msgid "From our burrow. Not stolen! Goblins get the blame for everything. Gentle shake, only gentle. {price}. Looking is free. Looking more, not free!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:445
msgid "Nettle's clan dug it up fair and square. Gentle shake only. {price}. You want to shake more? You pay more!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:446
msgid "Burrow chest. Smells of goblin. Is fine. {price}, and more every time you shake it different."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:447
msgid "Ooh, you like! Price go up: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:447
msgid "More shaking, more gold! {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:447
msgid "Hehe. {price} now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:448
msgid "A goblin of the hills, trading chests out of her clan's burrow (fairly: she'll tell you so). She only shakes gently, so she never prices what a gentle shake can't stir, and goblins charge for everything, looking included: each strength you try after your first puts her price up a tenth."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:451
msgid "Shiny! Shiny!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:451
msgid "Hehehe. Nettle's burrow gets a door!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:452
msgid "Pah! Nettle has other customers."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:453
msgid "Pah! Nettle sell it to someone with eyes."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:453
msgid "Your loss. Nettle's gain. Nettle always gains."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:454
msgid "Eek! Nettle's chest!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:454
msgid "Hehe, again! Again!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:455
msgid "You drop Nettle's chest? Price go up!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:459
msgid "Rook Varga"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:459
msgid "Rook"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:462
msgid "The Magpie's bounty, the biggest the Wardens have ever posted."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:463
msgid "Draws her bow left-handed."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:463
msgid "A hunter's clean hands: no ink."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:463
msgid "Rides in boots."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:465
msgid "Took it off an outlaws' camp on the forest road, for the Wardens' bounty. My scale says {pounds}. {price}. Gently: the mare spooks."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:466
msgid "The outlaws won't be needing it. {pounds} on my scale, and I price by the pound: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:467
msgid "Found it in a wolf den. The wolves had eaten whoever was carrying it. {pounds} on my scale. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:468
msgid "Wolves don't hoard, but their dinners did. {pounds}, to the half pound. {price}. Easy with it: the mare."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:469
msgid "A huntress who takes the Wardens' bounties, and sells what the outlaws had. She weighs every chest on her game scale and prices it by the pound, so light things (spells, gems) come cheap. Her chests hang on a mare who bolts at a hard shake: take the weight of what you heard from the scale's, and what's left is what never stirred."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:472
msgid "Good hunting."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:473
msgid "The mare's restless. I'm off."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:474
msgid "No matter. It'll sell at the next market."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:474 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:594
msgid "Fair enough."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:475
msgid "Easy! You'll have the mare bolting."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:475 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:595
msgid "Steady."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:476
msgid "Easy! You've upset the mare, and me. Half again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:480
msgid "Mother Sorrel"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:480
msgid "Sorrel"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:483
msgid "To keep the Guild's axes out of the Old Wood."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:484
msgid "Fingers green from her herbs."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:484
msgid "Goes barefoot, always."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:485
msgid "The Old Wood let this one go. I slept beside it and dreamt of {dream}. The oaks whispered its price: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:486
msgid "Moss grew on it for a hundred years. Last night I dreamt of {dream}, and of a price: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:487
msgid "The Old Wood's druid at Thornwick. Her price comes to her in a dream, and she always dreams true, in signs: of what the Wood warded in the chest, or else of the dearest thing in it. A magpie is coin, a thorn a weapon, a raven's wing a cloak, a river a potion, an owl a spell, a star a gem. If you can't hear what she dreamt of, it's warded: name it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:490
msgid "As the Wood wills."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:490
msgid "The oaks approve."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:491
msgid "The Wood is calling me home."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:492
msgid "The Wood is patient. So am I."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:492
msgid "Then it wasn't meant for you. Not yet."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:493
msgid "Mind the moss, child."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:493
msgid "The Wood felt that."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:494
msgid "The Wood felt that, child. So will your purse."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:498
msgid "Brother Cadoc"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:498
msgid "Cadoc"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:500
msgid "Bread for the poor at the abbey gate, and the Unopened kept off its steps."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:501
msgid "From the crypt of Saint Ide, by the Abbot's leave. A firm shake, but not hard, please: the saints are resting. {price}, for the poor."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:502
msgid "A brother's reliquary, three hundred years asleep. I gave it a firm shake, as is seemly. {price} feeds the gate for a week."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:503
msgid "The almoner of the abbey of Saint Ide, selling the crypt's chests to feed the poor at its gate. He shakes a chest firmly and won't have it shaken hard (half again if you do), so the holy cloaks a crypt chest is full of never make a sound for him, and go unpriced."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:506
msgid "Bless you. The gate eats tonight."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:506
msgid "Saint Ide thanks you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:507 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:511
msgid "Brother! The saints! Half again, for the sacrilege."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:508
msgid "Forgive me, I'm due at vespers."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:509
msgid "Another day, perhaps. The poor are patient. They have to be."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:509
msgid "Peace be with you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:510
msgid "Brother! Gently!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:510
msgid "Oh! Saint Ide preserve us."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:515
msgid "Corvin Tallow"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:515
msgid "Corvin"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:518
msgid "One more good season on the smugglers' road, and then a boat, and the sea."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:519
msgid "Packed in straw, so nothing clinked at the Wardens' toll. I gave it a firm shake. {price}, and no questions."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:520
msgid "Came up the smugglers' road. Don't ask whose. The straw muffles everything, but I gave it a firm shake. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:521
msgid "Runs brandy and chests past the Wardens' toll on the forest road, every chest packed in straw so nothing clinks: everything in it needs a strength harder to stir, and cloaks and spells won't stir at all. A firm shake, never a drop, and smugglers love a false bottom. Haggles. Now and then a chest he carries isn't his to sell."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:524
msgid "Pleasure. We never met."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:524
msgid "Done. Mind the Wardens."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:525
msgid "{price}, and you're robbing me."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:525
msgid "Tch. {price}, final."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:526
msgid "Hmph. Plenty of other buyers."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:526
msgid "I've a wagon to catch."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:527
msgid "Your loss. I was never here."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:527
msgid "Suit yourself. Forget my face."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:528
msgid "Quiet! Do you want the Wardens round?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:528
msgid "Easy. That's straw, not stone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:529
msgid "Quiet, you fool! That noise will cost you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:533
msgid "Aunt Hesper"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:533
msgid "Hesper"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:536
msgid "To marry off the whole county, and to know whose chests are whose: a matchmaker keeps every family's accounts."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:537
msgid "Ink on her fingers from the marriage contracts."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:537
msgid "Rides her pony in boots, village to village."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:538
msgid "A dowry, love, from a wedding that never was: {clue}, as ever. Shaken hard: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:539
msgid "The groom ran off to the Barrow. Her dowry: {clue}. Shaken hard: {price}. I've another match for her already."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:540
msgid "Thornwick's matchmaker, selling dowries from weddings that never happened. A Thornwick dowry always holds coin for luck, a cloak for warmth and a potion for health, and a bride often wards one of the three: whichever you can't hear is the warded one. Hesper shakes hard and prices what she hears, never what's warded."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:543
msgid "May it bring you luck."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:543
msgid "Mind you use it well, love."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:544
msgid "I've a match to make, love. Toodle-oo."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:545
msgid "Ah well. There's always another wedding."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:545
msgid "Not to your taste? Nor was the groom to hers."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:546
msgid "Mind the bride's things, love!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:546
msgid "Ooh! Careful."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:547
msgid "That's a bride's dowry, love! It'll cost you more now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:551 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:551
msgid "Flick"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:554
msgid "To be paid, to be fed, and never to be caught. Runs chests for the Magpie."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:555
msgid "It came my way, didn't it. {price}, quick. I can't stand about, mister."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:556
msgid "Don't ask where it's from and I won't ask what you'll do with it. {price}. Twenty seconds."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:557
msgid "A {colour} chest for {price}. Cheap, 'cause I'm in a hurry. Yes or no?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:558
msgid "A pickpocket of twelve who runs chests for the Magpie: cheap, priced by colour, and in a hurry (twenty seconds). Most of what Flick sells isn't Flick's to sell: lay a hand on it, and your mark goes cold. From Thornwick in, you can send for the Wardens."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:560
msgid "Ta. Never saw you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:560
msgid "Done. I'm off."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:561
msgid "Too slow, mister. I'm gone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:562
msgid "Someone'll have it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:563
msgid "Oi! Quiet!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:563
msgid "Careful! People are looking."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:564
msgid "Drop it again and the price goes up. And the Wardens come running."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:570
msgid "Bailiff Marrow"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:570
msgid "Marrow"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:572
msgid "The Guild's books balanced, and its friends served first."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:573
msgid "From a house the Guild sealed for tithe. A {colour} chest at the Guild's book price: {price}. The Guild doesn't haggle."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:574
msgid "Taken for tithe, and sold to the Guild's friends first. The book says a {colour} chest is {price}, whatever's in it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:575
msgid "The Gilded Guild's bailiff, who sells what it took for tithe to the Guild's friends first, at its book price: the chest's colour, nothing more. A third of it was seized, not sold, and won't open for anyone: lay a hand on it. He comes while the Guild counts you a friend."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:577
msgid "Entered in the book. Good day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:577
msgid "The Guild thanks its friends."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:578
msgid "I've three more houses to see to today."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:579
msgid "As you like. Someone else is a friend of the Guild."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:579 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:696
msgid "Noted."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:580
msgid "That's Guild property until it's paid for."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:581
msgid "Damage to Guild property is added to the price."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:585
msgid "Quartermaster Brandt"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:585
msgid "Brandt"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:587
msgid "The Wardens' store emptied, and the money in the widows' fund."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:588
msgid "Taken off a thief a year and a day ago, and nobody's claimed it. The Wardens' tariff is by the pound: {pounds}, so {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:589
msgid "Unclaimed, a year and a day: it's the Crown's to sell now. {pounds} on the toll scale, at the tariff: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:590
msgid "The Wardens' quartermaster at the Thornwick toll, selling what they took off thieves and nobody claimed in a year and a day. The Wardens' tariff is so much a pound, so heavy things come dear and light ones cheap. He comes while the Wardens count you a friend."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:592
msgid "For the widows' fund. Much obliged."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:592
msgid "Sold, by the tariff."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:593
msgid "The toll won't keep itself."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:594
msgid "It'll keep. It's kept a year already."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:595
msgid "Easy with the Crown's property."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:596
msgid "That's breakage. Breakage goes on the price."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:602
msgid "Ilse Varrow"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:602
msgid "Ilse"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:605
msgid "To be an archmage one day. Lately, to know what her mistress is building in the cellar."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:606
msgid "Archmage Orme's clearing out the Arcanum stores. The tag says: packed, {clue}. She says {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:607
msgid "This one's from the third cellar. I can read the tag, at least: {clue}. {price}, my mistress says."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:608
msgid "The Arcanum's apprentice, clearing its stores for her mistress. Every chest still has its packing tag, listing each kind of thing packed in it, and the archmages warded the most dangerous: a kind on the tag that you can't hear is warded. Prices by the chest's colour, as she's told."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:611
msgid "Oh good! Don't tell my mistress I was nervous."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:611
msgid "Thank you!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:612
msgid "I'm late! She'll turn me into something."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:613
msgid "Oh. She won't be pleased."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:613
msgid "That's all right. There's a whole cellar of them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:614
msgid "Careful! Some of those are cursed!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:614
msgid "Eep!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:615
msgid "She said to keep them in one piece! I'll have to ask more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:619
msgid "Archmage Thessaly Orme"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:619
msgid "Orme"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:621
msgid "To understand the Locking well enough to undo it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:622
msgid "From the Arcanum's oldest stores. {price}. Tell me exactly what's in it, and a third comes back to you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:623
msgid "A {colour} chest: {price}. Read it true, Keywright, and I'll return a third. I study how your kind hears."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:624
msgid "An archmage of the Arcanum who studies the Locking, and Keywrights. She prices by the chest's colour, and likes a wager: read her chest exactly right, every kind and every count, and she gives back a third of what you paid."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:626
msgid "Let us see."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:626
msgid "We shall see what you heard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:627
msgid "My engine won't build itself. Good day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:628
msgid "Prudent. Or timid. We shall never know."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:628
msgid "Another time, Keywright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:629
msgid "Hm. Bold."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:629
msgid "Fascinating. Do that again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:630
msgid "That chest is older than your great-grandmother. A third more, I think."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:634
msgid "Durgan Ironhand"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:634
msgid "Durgan"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:636
msgid "Ironroot's crown, locked in the Royal Treasury since the Locking; and a buyer for dwarf-gold the Guild won't let him sell."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:637
msgid "From the deep seam under Ironroot. Hard shake, with dwarf's hands. {price}. Not a coin of it to the Guild, mind."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:638
msgid "From Ironroot hold, sealed since my great-great-grandmother's day. I gave it a proper shake. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:639
msgid "A dwarf trader of Ironroot Street, who knows a weapon when he hears one. He prices weapons in full, everything else at half, and takes every tinkle for a diamond. He shakes hard, and haggles."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:641
msgid "Done. Back to the deep."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:641
msgid "Ha! Done."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:642
msgid "{price}. Any lower and I'll eat my helmet."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:642
msgid "{price}, and that's stone-solid."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:643
msgid "You take me for a fool? Good day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:644
msgid "Hmph. Your loss, surface-dweller."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:644
msgid "Back down the mine with it, then."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:645
msgid "Ha! Dwarf-made. It'll take worse than that."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:645
msgid "Watch it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:646
msgid "Mind my stone-work! That'll cost you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:650 scripts/Core/TaleBook.cs:1177
msgid "Lady Isaura Vell"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:650
msgid "Isaura"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:653
msgid "To keep the Vell house standing, despite her brother's debts."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:654
msgid "Grandmother's trick box. Her riddle's on the lid: \"{clue}\" {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:655
msgid "From the Vell strongroom, before my brother finds it: {price}. Grandmother's riddle: \"{clue}\""
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:656
msgid "A noblewoman of an old house gone poor, selling her grandmother's trick boxes before her brother can. Each lid has grandmother's riddle about one thing inside, and if she warded something, the riddle is about that. Solve it: if you can't hear the answer, it's warded. Prices by colour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:659
msgid "How delightful."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:659
msgid "Grandmother would approve."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:660
msgid "I have creditors at four. Do excuse me."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:661
msgid "Pity. Grandmother so loved a puzzle."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:661
msgid "Another time, perhaps."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:662
msgid "Goodness!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:662
msgid "Do be careful, that's a Vell."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:663
msgid "That is a Vell heirloom! The price has just gone up."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:667
msgid "Silas Brass"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:667
msgid "Brass"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:670
msgid "His money; and, though he'll never say it, to be thought kind."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:671
msgid "Pledged twenty years ago on Lantern Lane and never redeemed. The ticket says {articles}. A firm shake. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:672
msgid "Ticket four thousand and twelve: {articles}, it says. I price a lot kind by kind, at a firm shake. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:673
msgid "The pawnbroker of Lantern Lane, selling pledges nobody redeemed, often two or three of a kind. He prices one of each kind he hears and never counts how many. The pawn ticket counts every article pledged, false bottom and all, and he won't have pledges dropped: count what you hear against the ticket."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:676
msgid "Done. No refunds."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:676
msgid "Sold, as heard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:677 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:681
msgid "Not on my pledges! Half again, for the damage."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:678
msgid "Time is money, and you're spending mine."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:679
msgid "Back on the shelf it goes."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:679
msgid "As you like. Pledges keep."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:680
msgid "Mind the pledges!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:685
msgid "Master Quire"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:685
msgid "Quire"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:688
msgid "The Chest Roll kept true. Lately, to know why it says the Guild's chests aren't the Guild's."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:689
msgid "From the Royal Archive's vaults, with its ward-roll: {clue}. Unclaimed since the Locking. So much a rattle: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:690
msgid "The Chest Roll lists no owner for this one. The ward-roll reads {clue}, as far as I can make it out. I counted the rattles: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:691
msgid "The Royal Archivist, keeper of the Chest Roll, selling unclaimed vault chests with their ward-rolls. A roll names what was warded in its chest, its letters faded by three hundred years: read the name, and name its kind on your slip. A blank roll means nothing was warded. He counts the rattles at a firm shake and charges the same for each."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:694
msgid "Duly recorded."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:694
msgid "I'll enter it in the Roll."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:695
msgid "The Archive closes at six. Good day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:696
msgid "Very well. I'll file it under 'unsold'."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:697
msgid "Careful! That's Crown property."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:697
msgid "Oh dear."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:698
msgid "That is Crown property! I'll have to add a fee for that."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:702
msgid "Tilly Mudge"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:702
msgid "Tilly"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:705
msgid "To find the bell she hears tolling under the Aldwater on still nights."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:706
msgid "Out of the Aldwater mud at low tide! I shook it hard, and I'd bet my boots on what rustles. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:707
msgid "The river gives and the river takes. Shook it hard: spellbooks, potions, who knows! {price}. Heard the bell again last night."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:708
msgid "A mudlark who combs the Aldwater at low tide, shakes hard, and prices every rustle as a drowned wizard's spellbook. Her scroll cases are often full of river sand, which pours at the gentlest shake. Real parchment only rustles at a hard one."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:710
msgid "Mud's been good to me!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:710
msgid "The river provides."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:711
msgid "Tide's turning. I'm off."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:712
msgid "Back in the barrow, then."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:712
msgid "No skin off my nose."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:713
msgid "Ha! It's been through worse in the river."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:713
msgid "Oop!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:714
msgid "Oi! Mud or no mud, that's mine. It'll cost more now."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:718
msgid "Sir Rowan Gale"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:718
msgid "Rowan"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:720
msgid "His grandfather's sword, and his family's hall back from the Guild, which foreclosed on it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:721
msgid "A Gale war chest. If my grandfather's sword's in it, it's mine, and I'll pay you {fee} for it. The rest is yours for {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:722
msgid "From the siege of Harrowgate. Any blade in it is my family's: {fee} for the best. {price} for the chest."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:723
msgid "A knight without a war, whose family's hall the Guild foreclosed on. He's looking for his grandfather's sword. Prices by colour. If there are weapons in his chest, the best of them goes back to him for the price he names: value what's left."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:725
msgid "Honour is satisfied."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:725
msgid "For the Gales!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:726
msgid "I'm expected at the lists. Good day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:727
msgid "Then I shall keep looking."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:727
msgid "Another chest, another day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:728
msgid "Have a care, sir!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:728
msgid "Steady!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:729
msgid "Have a care with my grandfather's things! It'll cost you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:737 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:737
msgid "Tick"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:740
msgid "Errands run, gold gone down the Gate, and one day off in three hundred years."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:741
msgid "Fresh through the Gate, from the Maw's own hoard. {price}. And the sand's already running, mortal."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:742
msgid "Errand for the Maw. A {colour} chest: {price}. Tick, tock."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:743
msgid "An imp courier with an hourglass, selling from the Maw's hoard. Prices by colour and never looks inside, and gives you twelve seconds to decide. Things from the Maw's hoard are often better than their chest's colour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:745
msgid "Delicious."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:745
msgid "A pleasure, mortal."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:746
msgid "Too slow! Back through the Gate I go."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:747
msgid "Pfft. Your loss, mortal."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:747
msgid "Fine. Someone in the Emporium has more sense."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:748
msgid "Hee! Again!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:748
msgid "Clumsy mortal."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:749
msgid "Careful, mortal! Breakages cost extra."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:753
msgid "Lord Sallow"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:753
msgid "Sallow"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:755
msgid "To win every bargain he makes. He always has."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:756
msgid "From the Maw's hoard. {price}, a pittance. My only condition: the dearest thing inside is mine."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:757
msgid "A bargain, mortal: {price}. When it opens, I take the best of it. Everything else is yours."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:758
msgid "A devil of the old law, who deals in bargains. His price is low, but the dearest thing inside is his. A chest of many middling things suits his deal; one grand thing and little else doesn't."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:760
msgid "Signed and sealed."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:760
msgid "A pleasure doing business. It always is."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:761
msgid "My time is worth more than yours, mortal."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:762
msgid "Another time. There is always another time."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:762
msgid "How very wise of you. Or was it?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:763
msgid "Mind my bones."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:763
msgid "Tsk."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:764
msgid "Damaged goods cost more, mortal. Read the small print."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:768 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:768
msgid "Skrae"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:771
msgid "Out: away from the Gate, and the Maw, for good. It has heard enough."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:772
msgid "Shaken gently, then hard: {price}. Then I clicked, like a bat. The echoes: {clue}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:773
msgid "I hear every coin in the realm, and every word the Maw says. {price}. My echoes: {clue}. Wards can't stop an echo."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:774
msgid "A demon with ears like a bat, who has heard enough of the Maw. It shakes a chest gently, then hard, and prices what it hears, fairly. Then it clicks and listens to the echoes, which come back off everything inside, warded or not: round is coin, long a weapon, soft a cloak, hollow a potion, flat a spell, tiny a gem. An echo you can't hear is warded."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:777
msgid "Fair."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:777
msgid "You won't regret it. Probably."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:778
msgid "I hear someone counting gold elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:779
msgid "I heard that coming."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:779
msgid "Hm. Fair enough."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:780
msgid "Ow! My ears!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:780
msgid "Loud. Very loud."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:781
msgid "My ears! That will cost you."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:785
msgid "Countess Vey"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:785
msgid "the Countess"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:788
msgid "To keep up appearances at court, a jewel at a time. Some of her gems are paste, and she knows which."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:789
msgid "From my strongroom. My gems, and whatever my maid packed. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:790
msgid "The gems alone are worth {price}, I'm told. The rest I couldn't say. My maid packs."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:791
msgid "A countess of the court who knows her own jewels and nothing else: she prices her gems at what she paid for them, and whatever else her maid packed comes free. Some of her gems are paste, and she won't have a lodestone near them (half again if you try)."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:793
msgid "Charming."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:793
msgid "Do look after them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:794
msgid "A lodestone? On MY gems? Half again, for the insult."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:795
msgid "I'm expected at court. Good day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:796
msgid "How very disappointing."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:796
msgid "Well. Someone at court will have it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:797
msgid "My gems!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:797
msgid "Must you?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:798
msgid "My gems! Half again, for the fright."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:802
msgid "Madame Zell"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:802
msgid "Zell"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:805
msgid "To be right, and to be paid for it. The cards don't lie; Madame Zell doesn't either."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:806
msgid "A courtier's chest, sold for his gambling debts. Three from the Locking's deck: {clue}. {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:807
msgid "The cards chose this one for you, dear. {clue}. A {colour} chest: {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:808
msgid "The court's cartomancer. She draws three cards from the Locking's own deck for each chest: a suit drawn twice is what the ward holds (Coins, Swords for weapons, Mantles for cloaks, Cups for potions, Wands for spells, Stars for gems); three different suits, and nothing's warded. Prices by colour."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:811
msgid "The cards are never wrong."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:811
msgid "As it was foretold."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:812
msgid "The cards say I'm wanted elsewhere."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:813
msgid "The cards did say you might."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:813
msgid "As you wish, dear."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:814
msgid "I didn't see that coming. How rare."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:814
msgid "Oh!"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:815
msgid "The cards warned me about you. Half again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:819 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:819
msgid "Gilt"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:822
msgid "The Maw's gilded iron sold as gold, so the Gate's gold buys more of the realm."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:823
msgid "Out of the Maw's hoard, friend, through a crack in the Gate. I'm leaving town tonight, so {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:824
msgid "Hoard goods, very rare. Gold and gems, every one of them. For you, just {price}."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:825
msgid "The Maw's fence. He knows exactly what's in his chests, because he packed the demon gold himself: gilded iron sold as gold and gems, cheap. What's real comes cheap; the fakes are worth nothing."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:827
msgid "Wonderful! No refunds."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:827
msgid "A pleasure. I really must be going."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:828
msgid "Can't stay. People to avoid."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:829
msgid "Your loss, friend. Your very great loss."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:829
msgid "Suit yourself. I was never here."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:830
msgid "Easy, friend! Easy."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:830
msgid "Whoa there."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:831
msgid "Easy, friend! That'll cost a little extra."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:835
msgid "Old Aldo"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:835
msgid "Aldo"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:838
msgid "A Keywright he can trust with the one chest that matters."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:839
msgid "From an old house with a great many cellars. I've no idea what's in it. You tell me, and whatever you say it holds is my price."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:840
msgid "Old things from an old house. Name what's inside: that's the price. Name it truly and I'll take a quarter off."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:841
msgid "A tired old man in a plain cloak, with a very fine ring. He doesn't know what's in his chests: his price is whatever your slip says. Read it exactly and he takes a quarter off; read it wrong and you pay what it really holds, and a quarter more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:843
msgid "Well. We shall see."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:843
msgid "Hm. Let's see what you heard."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:844
msgid "I'm needed elsewhere. Another day."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:845
msgid "Another day, then. I'll be back."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:845
msgid "Hm. A careful one. Good."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:846
msgid "Steady. It's older than both of us."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:846
msgid "Oh my."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:847
msgid "Steady! That was my grandfather's. I'll want a little more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:851
msgid "Avarax, the Gilded Maw"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:851
msgid "the Maw"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:854
msgid "Out."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:855
msgid "A trifle from my hoard. One coin. All I ask is that you open it here, where I can see."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:856
msgid "One coin, little Keywright. And then everyone in this city will want twice as much today. Isn't that fun?"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:857
msgid "The demon of greed himself, in a borrowed body dripping with rings. He sells a chest for one coin, but greed is catching: buy it, and everyone who comes to your counter after him that day asks twice as much."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:859
msgid "Yesss."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:859
msgid "Open it. Let me see."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:860
msgid "I have all the time in the world. You don't."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:861
msgid "Clever little thing."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:861
msgid "Mm. Another day, then. There are so many days."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:862
msgid "Careful. I break things too."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:862
msgid "Ha."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:863
msgid "Careful. Greed always wants more."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:875
msgid "Sergeant Hollis"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:875
msgid "Hollis"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:876
msgid "Thieves caught and chests home; and to know why the Guild's foreclosed chests won't open for anyone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:877
msgid "The Wardens' sergeant at the Thornwick toll: posts the wanted notices, searches the market, pays a finder's share for a stolen chest sent home."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:881
msgid "Tobias Fenn"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:881
msgid "Tobias"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:882
msgid "To know where the tithe goes, and not to vanish for asking."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:883
msgid "A clerk in the Gilded Guild's counting-house, with ink to the elbows and doubts he shouldn't have."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:887
msgid "Mistress Aubel"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:887
msgid "Aubel"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:888
msgid "Every marked child in the county, for the Guild's counting-houses."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:889
msgid "A Guild Mark-Finder, who tests children's hands at every fair and takes the marked ones \"into the Guild's care\"."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:893
msgid "Wynn Hollow"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:893
msgid "Wynn"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:894
msgid "Her son kept out of the Guild's counting-houses."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:895
msgid "Pip's mother, the mill's washerwoman."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:899
msgid "Harl Caskett"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:899
msgid "Caskett"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:900
msgid "The Old Wood's oak, felled and sold, on the Guild's account."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:901
msgid "The Gilded Guild's timber factor, with a deed for the Old Wood and a pen for whoever will witness it."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:905
msgid "The Hawthorn Lady"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:905
msgid "the Hawthorn Lady"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:906
msgid "The Wood's oaks left standing; and a promise, kept."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:907
msgid "One of the fair folk of the Old Wood. She never used gold, and trades in promises."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:911
msgid "Lord Cassian Vell"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:911
msgid "Cassian"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:913
msgid "Tonight's stake at cards. Tomorrow's, too."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:914
msgid "Lady Isaura's brother, a gambler, selling his sister's chests cheap. They aren't his to sell."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:915
msgid "Splendid. The tables await."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:915
msgid "Done. Not a word to my sister."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:916
msgid "Your loss. Someone will want it before the cards start."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:916
msgid "Pity."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:921
msgid "Jasper Wick"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:921
msgid "Jasper"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:922
msgid "A good ear, a low price, and no licence: and never to see the inside of a Guild counting-house."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:923
msgid "A hedge-wright: a Keywright without the Guild's licence, as Bram was for twenty years, trading from a cart."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:927
msgid "Sir Aldwin Gale"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:927
msgid "Sir Aldwin"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:928
msgid "His blade in his family's hands, and then to rest."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:929
msgid "A knight who fell on Brindle Field the year before the Locking, and has walked it since."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:933
msgid "Martha Dunning"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:933
msgid "Martha"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:934
msgid "Thornwick's roads free and its market open, and the Old Wood left standing."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:935
msgid "A Thornwick weaver, standing for reeve against the Guild's money with nothing but a loom and a loud voice."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:939
msgid "Sister Agathe"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:939
msgid "Agathe"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:940
msgid "Every chest left shut, as Saint Ide meant them; and to know who pays for the Unopened's bread."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:941
msgid "A preacher of the Unopened, the abbey's zealots, who say every chest opened feeds the Maw."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:945
msgid "Mother Tansy"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:945
msgid "Tansy"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:946
msgid "Her money back, with a third on top, on the morning she said."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:947
msgid "A moneylender of Lantern Lane, who lends to anyone short for the Guild and collects from everyone."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:951
msgid "Mistress Ashby"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:951
msgid "Ashby"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:953
msgid "Her daughter's dowry, which the Corlews say is theirs."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:954
msgid "A Thornwick widow whose daughter was to marry a Corlew, until the wedding wasn't."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:955
msgid "There. The ward agrees with me."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:956 scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:965
msgid "Then the court will hear it again."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:960
msgid "Hal Corlew"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:960
msgid "Corlew"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:962
msgid "His sister's dowry, which the Ashbys say is theirs."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:963
msgid "A Thornwick carter whose sister was to marry into the Ashbys, until the wedding wasn't."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:964
msgid "Knew it. Told them."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:969
msgid "Jory Kettle"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:969
msgid "Jory"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:970
msgid "To pay you back for his freedom, and to see the Guild's debt-houses emptied."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:971
msgid "Ada's son, two years in the Guild's debt-house for his father's tithe."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1005
msgid "a farmer at Brindle"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1005
msgid "the Crossed Keys"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1005
msgid "the miller's wife"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1006
msgid "a carter on the forest road"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1006
msgid "a Thornwick family"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1006
msgid "the abbey's gatehouse"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1007
msgid "a Crownhold merchant"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1007
msgid "Lord Harrow's household"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1007
msgid "a family on Lantern Lane"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1007
msgid "a chapel by the Aldwater"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1008
msgid "a lady of the court"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1008
msgid "a palace steward"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1008
msgid "a banker of the Emporium"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1008
msgid "a courtier's widow"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1022
msgid "Gods! It just... burst open! Keep the singing thing, then. The rest is going home with me."
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1026
msgid "one"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1026
msgid "two"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1026
msgid "three"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1026
msgid "four"
msgstr ""

#: scripts/Core/Sellers.cs:1026
msgid "five"
